## 3. Enumeration method and the completeness guard

"100 %" is defined mechanically, not by reading, and the guard is non-tautological. `tools/re-bpmn-js/enumerate.mjs` (Node, zero dependencies, no network) extracts the observable surface from the pinned sources with line/regex rules. Independently, `tools/re-bpmn-js/extract-ast.mjs` enumerates the same families from the same sources with the TypeScript compiler API (`ts.createProgram` over the checkouts, AST visitors; no shared code with `enumerate.mjs`, no regex extraction). The two extractors share no perimeter list, constant or function: every perimeter the guard checks (didi modules, providers, renderer maps, moddle descriptors, service classes, examples) is derived by `extract-ast.mjs` from the source structure (export shapes, registration calls, JSON imports, didi service registrations), never copied from the generator; the only common vocabulary is the output format itself (`detail` strings and family names, fixed by §3.1). `tools/re-bpmn-js/verify.mjs` compares the inventory against the AST extraction only — it never imports `enumerate.mjs` — and asserts an exact bijection between the two enumerations plus, for every shared key, equality of `source.path` and `detail`, plus schema, source-resolution and proof-resolution checks on the inventory. A key present on one side and absent on the other, or found at different sources or with different details, is printed (both directions, both values) and fails the guard. **"100 %" therefore means: 100 % of the items two independent extractors agree on, at the same source and with the same detail, under the conventions below.** Anything the conventions cannot see is listed as a limit (§3.3), never silently dropped.

### 3.1 Counting conventions (one entry per distinct key, per family)

| Family | Mechanical definition | Extractor anchor |
|---|---|---|
| `module` | Every `index.js` under `lib/` of bpmn-js and diagram-js (one didi module each) | directory walk in `enumerate.mjs` (`extractModules`) |
| `command` | Distinct ids from the `Modeling.getHandlers()` maps, `commandStack.registerHandler('…')` and `commandStack.execute('…')` | `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/modeling/Modeling.js` (`getHandlers`), `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/modeling/Modeling.js` (`getHandlers`) |
| `rule` | Distinct `addRule('…')` action names (array forms expanded) | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/rules/BpmnRules.js` (`init`) |
| `palette` | Keys returned by bpmn-js `PaletteProvider.getPaletteEntries` | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/palette/PaletteProvider.js` (`getPaletteEntries`) |
| `context-pad` | Distinct entry keys assigned in bpmn-js `ContextPadProvider` (single- and multi-element) + the multi-element `align-elements` entry | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/context-pad/ContextPadProvider.js` (`getContextPadEntries`); `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/align-elements/AlignElementsContextPadProvider.js:70` |
| `replace-menu` | Distinct `actionName`s actually offered by `ReplaceMenuProvider`: `replaceWith('…')` calls (default `replace-with-<id>`, overridden where stated) + `SEQUENCE_FLOW` literals; commented-out options excluded | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/replace/ReplaceOptions.js` (e.g. `replace-with-sequence-flow` at line 248) |
| `popup-menu` | Provider registrations (`registerProvider('…', …)`, disambiguated by provider file when an id repeats) + header entries + align/distribute entries | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/popup-menu/ReplaceMenuProvider.js:89`; `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/align-elements/AlignElementsMenuProvider.js:45`; `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/distribute-elements/DistributeElementsMenuProvider.js:35` |
| `keyboard` | Editor-action names in `SHORTCUTS_KEY_BINDINGS` + diagram-js default `addListener` actions (every listener kept in the detail, `KeyboardUtil` `KEYS_*` groups merged into the matching action detail, never entries) + every registered `EditorActions` action + keys handled without an editor action (`searchPad:*` isKey keys, `handTool:Space` hold key) | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/keyboard/BpmnKeyboardBindings.js` (`SHORTCUTS_KEY_BINDINGS`); `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/keyboard/KeyboardBindings.js:165,180` (both `stepZoom` listeners); `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/search-pad/SearchPad.js:153`; `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/hand-tool/HandTool.js:186` |
| `event` | Distinct EventBus names from `fire('…')`, `.on('…')`, `.once('…')` and their array forms (arrays may span lines) over both `lib/` trees, + `_emit`/`_fire` helper calls (prefix resolved from each helper definition, template literals included), string-constant event names, `InteractionEvents` table values, `CommandStack` lifecycle qualifiers and `Dragging` helper types; JSDoc lines (starting with `*`) excluded; names ending in `.` kept once and flagged `dynamicPrefix` | e.g. `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/interaction-events/InteractionEvents.js:135`; `RE:diagram-js/lib/command/CommandStack.js:383`; `RE:bpmn-js/lib/BaseViewer.js:766` |
| `config` | `BaseViewerOptions`/`DiagramOptions` typedef fields + `config.*` didi injection keys + every DI-config read qualified by its file's injection (`config.<feature>.<prop>`); files without a `config.*` injection have no DI config and are skipped | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/BaseViewer.js` (`BaseViewerOptions` typedef); `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js:2325` (`config.bpmnRenderer`) |
| `renderer` | Keys of the `BpmnRenderer` `handlers` map (including `label`), `eventIconRenderers` map and `taskMarkerRenderers` map | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js` (`handlers`, from line 1318; `label` line 2310; markers from line 809) |
| `moddle-type` | Types and enumerations of the five JSON descriptors the moddle entry registers (bpmn, bpmndi, di, dc, bioc); enumerations read `literalValues`, types report `superClass` and `extends` | `RE:bpmn-moddle/lib/simple.js:7` (JSON package imports); `RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn/json/bpmn.json` (enumerations from line 2822) |
| `api` | Public (non-`_`) methods of every didi `type` service class plus the entry classes directly under `lib/`: `Class.prototype.<m>` assignments and constructor `this.<m> = function/<fn>` assignments; service classes resolved from `index.js` registrations, never from a class list | e.g. `RE:bpmn-js/lib/BaseViewer.js:220` (`importXML`); `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/clipboard/Clipboard.js:7` (`get`) |
| `example` | Top-level `bpmn-js-examples` directories whose `README.md` carries a markdown heading (upstream tombstones carry none); detail is that heading | `RE:bpmn-js-examples/` (26 directories; 3 tombstones excluded) |

Each inventory entry carries: `id` (`RE.<family>.<slug>`, stable), `family`, `key`, `source` (`path:line` in `RE:`), `behaviour` (observable input → output / interaction → effect), `acceptance` (a differential test scenario), `target` (`graph` / `diagram-core` / `diagram-canvas` / `ds-component` / `new-module`), `status` (`covered` / `partial` / `missing`) with `proof` (`path:line` in `WT:`), and `priority` (`P0` blocking, `P1` editing parity, `P2` polish). [JUDGMENT] The `target`/`priority` assignments and the `partial` thresholds are this spec's mapping, defined in §4.1; the extraction itself is judgement-free.

### 3.2 Guard output (measured in this worktree)

```console
$ node tools/re-bpmn-js/enumerate.mjs
wrote docs/re/bpmn-js-inventory.json entries=1237
$ node tools/re-bpmn-js/verify.mjs
COMPLETENESS GUARD: PASS entries=1237 astExtracted=1237 bijection=exact sourcePath=exact detail=exact
byFamily={"module":92,"command":33,"rule":13,"palette":15,"context-pad":19,"replace-menu":74,"popup-menu":17,"keyboard":30,"event":208,"config":41,"renderer":58,"moddle-type":174,"api":437,"example":26}
astByFamily={"module":92,"command":33,"rule":13,"palette":15,"context-pad":19,"replace-menu":74,"popup-menu":17,"keyboard":30,"event":208,"config":41,"renderer":58,"moddle-type":174,"api":437,"example":26}
```

The guard fails (exit 1) on: an AST-extracted item without an entry, an entry without an AST-extracted item (both listed), a `source.path` or `detail` disagreement on a shared key (both values listed), duplicate ids, a `source` or `proof` that does not resolve to a real `path:line`, or a missing/short `behaviour`/`acceptance`. As a control, the guard run against the pre-correction inventory (727 entries) fails with `onlyInAst=257 onlyInInventory=74`, and against single-entry tampered copies it names the exact missing, invented, re-sourced or re-detailed key (Annexes B–C). Re-running `enumerate.mjs` after any source or mapping change and then `verify.mjs` is the required loop; a green guard is a precondition for quoting any coverage figure from the inventory.

### 3.3 Limits of the enumeration (what "100 %" does not claim)

1. **Runtime-built names.** Event names assembled by concatenation (`commandStack.` + id, `drag.`, `keyboard.`, `popupMenu.`, `popupMenu.getProviders.`) appear once as `dynamicPrefix` entries. Their concrete suffixed forms are not statically enumerable; the harness (§8) must log them at runtime to extend the guard.
2. **The `color` moddle package (source-gap).** bpmn-moddle registers six packages; five have JSON descriptors in this checkout (163 types + 11 enumerations, counted as 174 `moddle-type` entries; enumerations are entries, not types). The sixth, `color` (3 types per the A′ spec), is imported from the external `bpmn-in-color-moddle` package (`RE:bpmn-moddle/lib/simple.js:12`), whose files are absent (no `node_modules`, no built `dist`). It is recorded in the inventory `meta.sourceGaps`, not counted. The A′ total of 166 types = 163 counted here + 3 `color`.
3. **Behaviour behind a key.** Extraction proves a key exists at a `path:line`; the *semantics* behind it (e.g. the full `canConnect` decision tree in `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/rules/BpmnRules.js`) are specified per family in §5 and proven only by the differential harness, not by the inventory.
4. **CSS, fonts and assets.** bpmn-font icons, `bpmn-js.css`/`diagram-js.css` class behaviour and the powered-by watermark rendering are observable but not key-enumerable; they are covered as renderer/config entries and by the visual arm of the harness (§8.4), and listed in §11 as residual surface.
5. **Specs as behaviour.** `*.spec.ts` files are excluded from extraction (they are tests, including doc-example event names such as `foo`); JSDoc example lines are likewise excluded from the `event` family.

## 4. Inventory summary and current coverage

### 4.1 How status was assigned [JUDGMENT, applied mechanically]

- `covered`: the behaviour is fully present in our stack today, citable at a `path:line`. **No entry qualifies.** This is a measured result, not a rhetorical one: the DS has no BPMN editor, and each candidate analogue is partial by its own README (see the proofs in the inventory).
- `partial`: a generic mechanism exists that covers a proper subset (e.g. `diagram-core` create/move/delete occurrences for `shape.create`; the `diagram-canvas` camera for `canvas.viewbox.changed`; graph edges for `bpmn:SequenceFlow`). The proof names the mechanism; the missing subset is what the lots in §9 must close.
- `missing`: no mechanism. The proof points at the document that records the gap (package README "What is not covered yet", or the skeleton's `NOT declared` notes at `WT:packages/diagram-core/src/profiles/skeletons.ts`, `NOT declared`).

