## Annex B — Gemini review: corrections applied / refused

Independent review: `.ds-scrap/re-reviews/bpmnjs-gemini-review.md` (Gemini 4 Argon High, read-only, verdict "fusionnable après corrections", 12 numbered corrections). Each correction was re-verified against the pinned sources before any change; the inventory effect was then measured by the two-extractor guard (§3.2), not asserted. "Applied" means the corrected enumeration/spec text is in this revision and the guard passes on it; "refused" means the claim does not hold against the source, with the counter-evidence cited. Several review line citations refer to a pre-revision layout of this spec and no longer resolve; those are marked *stale citation* and the substance was still checked.

| # | Correction (short form) | Verdict | Evidence and measured effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Missing `SPEC_EVOL_GD_BPMN_MODDLE_COVERAGE.md` + migration-plan D7 reference | **Obsolete, applied as alignment** | The A′ spec is on `main` since #164 (`96fc690b`); this branch was rebased on it. §7 now cites it on `main` and states D7′ (A′ spec §1.2; `spec/SPEC_EVOL_DS_JSON_RENDER_STANDARD.md` §18.4, #168): xyflow/elkjs allowed under qualification, bpmn-js only through `bpmn-canvas`, bpmn-moddle test-only. Step A of `WT:docs/graph-dataviz-migration-plan.md:7,11` keeps its status and is explicitly superseded for DS parity implementation only (§7). |
| 2 | Moddle counts, 11 missing enumerations, phantom `bioc.json` | **Applied in part; figures refused** | Enumerations applied: +11 entries (`bpmn` 9 from `RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn/json/bpmn.json:2822`, first at line 2824; `bpmndi` 2 from line 158), `moddle-type` 163 → 174, types unchanged. Refused: the review's per-file type counts (139/6/7/11) — measured 137/6/11/7 plus `bioc` 2, agreeing with the A′ registry count (`spec/SPEC_EVOL_GD_BPMN_MODDLE_COVERAGE.md` §3.1: 137/6/7/11/2/3 = 166); and the phantom claim — `RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn-io/json/bioc.json` exists with 2 types (`ColoredShape`/`ColoredEdge`, `stroke`/`fill`), and `MANIFEST.md` (7 lines) contains no line-19 citation. The quoted spec figures ("150/7/3/9") do not occur in this spec (*stale citation*). Legacy `stroke`/`fill` handling is cited at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/modeling/cmd/SetColorHandler.js:161` (`ensureLegacySupport`). |
| 3 | Missing context-pad `align-elements` | **Applied** | `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/align-elements/AlignElementsContextPadProvider.js:70`. `context-pad` 18 → 19. |
| 4 | Replace/popup menus: 3 SequenceFlow options, 6 header entries, 6 align + 2 distribute entries, hidden Distribute provider, dead `none-boundary-event` | **Applied (family redefined on measured options)** | `replace-menu` now counts the `actionName`s `ReplaceMenuProvider` actually offers from `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/replace/ReplaceOptions.js` (SequenceFlow literals at lines 248/253/258; commented-out gateways excluded): 74 measured options (review said 73; the extra unit is the distinct `replace-with-none-intermediate-throw` override alongside `replace-with-none-intermediate-throwing`). Header entries at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/popup-menu/ReplaceMenuProvider.js:527–646` (6), align entries from `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/align-elements/AlignElementsMenuProvider.js:19` (6), distribute entries at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/distribute-elements/DistributeElementsMenuProvider.js:70,80` (2), providers disambiguated by file (`ReplaceMenuProvider.js:89`, `AlignElementsMenuProvider.js:45`, `DistributeElementsMenuProvider.js:35`): `popup-menu` 2 → 17, `replace-menu` 70 → 74. `none-boundary-event` removed: it exists as a catalog atom (`RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/popup-menu/PopupEntries.js:234`) but is referenced nowhere else in `lib/` and never offered by `ReplaceMenuProvider` — recorded as a dead atom, not an invented key. |
| 5 | Renderer: `label` handler + 7 task markers (+ icon renderers) | **Applied and extended; one figure refused** | `label` at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js:2310`, markers at lines 810–933, icons from line 467. Measured maps: 39 handlers (including `label` and `bpmn:ReceiveTask` at line 1938 — missed by both the old extractor, space before the colon, and the review), 12 `eventIconRenderers`, 7 `taskMarkerRenderers`: `renderer` 37 → 58, `detail` distinguishes the three maps. Refused: the review's "26 handlers" subtotal, which no counting of the `handlers` map reproduces (39 measured). |
| 6 | Keyboard: second `stepZoom` listener, arrow navigation, search-pad, 6 unbound editor actions | **Applied** | Both `stepZoom` listeners kept in the entry detail (`RE:diagram-js/lib/features/keyboard/KeyboardBindings.js:165,180`); arrow navigation (`RE:diagram-js/lib/navigation/keyboard-move/KeyboardMove.js:33`, `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/keyboard-move-selection/KeyboardMoveSelection.js:84`) arrives through the `moveCanvas`/`moveSelection` actions (`RE:diagram-js/lib/features/editor-actions/EditorActions.js:181,187`); bpmn actions at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/editor-actions/BpmnEditorActions.js:103,114,130,156`; search-pad keys (`Escape`/`Enter`/`ArrowUp`/`ArrowDown`) from `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/search-pad/SearchPad.js`. `keyboard` 23 → 33 (+6 actions, +4 search-pad). |
| 7 | Events: InteractionEvents table, CommandStack lifecycle, Dragging types | **Applied with corrected counts** | Table at `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/interaction-events/InteractionEvents.js:135`, lifecycle in `RE:diagram-js/lib/command/CommandStack.js:383` (qualifiers called at lines 435–468, `changed` at 245/507), drag types in `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/dragging/Dragging.js`. Net `event` 151 → 180 (+29): only 2 of the 8 `element.*` names were actually missing (6 already captured), +9 `commandStack.*` qualifiers, +8 `drag.*` types (including `rejected`/`hover`/`out`/`init`, not listed by the review), +10 names from multi-line `.on([…])` arrays neither count had listed. Per-command `commandStack.<cmd>.<phase>` forms stay runtime-built under the `commandStack.` dynamic prefix (§3.3). |
| 8 | API services missing; module truncation and entry classes | **Applied in part; one sub-claim refused** | API extended to `Modeling` (bpmn `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/modeling/Modeling.js:112–321`, 15 methods; diagram 26 methods), `ElementRegistry`, `EventBus`, `CommandStack`, `Overlays`, `Selection`, `EditorActions`: `api` 49 → 131 (+82). The `services.slice(0, 8)` truncation is removed (module details now list every service, e.g. all modelling behaviours). Refused: no entry-class module exists to remove — `enumerate.mjs` walked `index.js` files only and the inventory contains no `RE.module.…baseviewer…` entry; the review's sampled `RE.module.bpmn-js-baseviewer-js` does not occur in `docs/re/bpmn-js-inventory.json`. |
| 9 | Label/style types marked `partial`; 3 dead examples counted as scenarios | **Applied** | `dc:Font`, `bpmndi:BPMNLabel`, `bpmndi:BPMNLabelStyle`, `di:Label`, `di:LabeledEdge`, `di:LabeledShape`, `di:Style`, `di:Extension` are now `missing`: `WT:packages/diagram-canvas/src/scene.ts:19` explicitly excludes labels (text measurement), so the former `partial` proof was not valid. The 3 tombstone examples (README only, `> Removed as of bpmn-js@0.27.0.`) are excluded from the family and recorded in `meta.sourceGaps`: `example` 29 → 26. Related sampled claims checked: `rule connection.create` was already `missing` (review's `partial` claim refused — it does not occur as `partial` in the inventory); the `element.setColor` behaviour text now states the `SetColorHandler` post-execute writes (`background-color`/`border-color`, `bioc` aliases, `BPMNLabel` colour). |
| 10 | Renderer independence: xyflow/WebGL adapters, camera conflict, explicit Bounds | **Applied (spec)** | New §5.7: one scene→adapter contract for xyflow (step A) and `@sentropic/graph` (step B), camera conversion confined to the graph adapter (persisted origin reading at `WT:packages/diagram-canvas/src/transform.ts:27` vs centre reading at `WT:packages/diagram-canvas/README.md:62`), explicit `dc:Bounds` sizing overriding text-fitted `boxDimensions` (`WT:packages/graph/src/render-geometry.ts:173`). DOM-returning reference APIs map to abstract handles/synthesised SVG (§5.5), never to DOM parity. Lots L3/L5/L7 carry the adapter gates. |
| 11 | Harness: pure-Node claim, tolerances, font metric | **Applied as hardening; premise refused** | No "pure Node, no browser for F1–F4" statement exists in this spec (*stale citation*): §8.4 already ran both sides in headless Chrome. Hardened with the measured reason the oracle needs a browser (`getBBox` `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js:1829`, `getPointAtLength` line 1795, Karma `ChromeHeadless` at `RE:bpmn-js/package.json:25`, `RE:bpmn-js/test/config/karma.unit.js:12`): live reference in Chromium or replayed versioned JSON fixtures in Node, pinned font metric (`Arial, sans-serif` 12 px, `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/TextRenderer.js:40`) before label bounds join the ±1 px gate. |
| 12 | Clean room: PathMap licence risk | **Applied (spec)** | §10 now explicitly prohibits copying, transcribing or transforming the path strings of `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/PathMap.js` into DS packages (watermark clause, `RE:bpmn-js/LICENSE`) and requires clean-room icon geometry from the BPMN 2.0 shapes or documented MIT-only sources. The migration-plan dependency contradiction is resolved by the D7′ statement in §7. |

Beyond the 12 corrections, the AST cross-check revealed gaps the review had not listed, all fixed in the same regeneration: `renderer` +`bpmn:ReceiveTask` (see #5), `config` 32 → 45 (every `config.*`/`this._config.*` read now counted, e.g. renderer colour defaults in `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js:123`), `event` multi-line `.on([…])` names (see #7), and untruncated module service lists (see #8). The guard's control runs: pre-correction inventory `FAIL (331)` with `onlyInAst=257 onlyInInventory=74`; single-entry removal or invention each fail naming the exact key; the corrected inventory passes (§3.2). No correction required touching `.track/`, and none was applied to shared docs or registration files.

