## Annex C — Gemini review round 2: corrections applied / refused

Second-round review: `.ds-scrap/re-reviews/bpmnjs-gemini-review-r2.md` (verdict "fusionnable après corrections", §4 lists 5 corrections). Each point was re-verified against the pinned sources before any change; the inventory effect was then measured by the two-extractor guard (§3.2), not asserted. Numbering follows the review's §4; §1/§3 findings that duplicate a §4 point are judged under that point, and the two sub-counts the review under-measured are refused with evidence under C3.

| # | Correction (short form) | Verdict | Evidence and measured effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| C1 | `moddle-type`: read `literalValues`, report `extends` | **Applied** | Enumerations name the value list `literalValues` (`RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn/json/bpmn.json:2884`, `RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn/json/bpmndi.json:159`); `bioc` types use `extends` (`RE:bpmn-moddle/resources/bpmn-io/json/bioc.json:8,24`). Both extractors now read `literalValues` (falling back to `values`) and append `extends:` to the type detail: the 11 enumerations show their values (e.g. `bpmn:AdHocOrdering` → `Parallel, Sequential`) and `bioc:ColoredShape`/`ColoredEdge` show `extends: bpmndi:BPMNShape`/`bpmndi:BPMNEdge`. `moddle-type` stays 174 (details only). |
| C2 | `config`: qualify reads by the file's didi injection, drop false top-level keys | **Applied** | Injections are declared per file (e.g. `RE:bpmn-js/lib/draw/BpmnRenderer.js:2325` `config.bpmnRenderer`, `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/grid-snapping/GridSnapping.js:185` `config.gridSnapping`); a `config.<prop>` read in such a file receives that sub-object, so reads are now stored as `config.<feature>.<prop>`. The 18 flat keys are gone (no `config.provider` — `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/popup-menu/PopupMenu.js:313` reads the open menu's descriptor, whose method is not constructor-forwarded — no `config.size/style/align/padding` — `RE:diagram-js/lib/util/Text.js:374` has no `config.*` injection and is skipped — and no flattened `config.active/autoFocus/bind/defaultFillColor/getContent/…`). `HoverTooltip` add-callbacks stay excluded for the same reason (no injection, `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/hover-tooltip/HoverTooltip.js:56`). `config` 45 → 41 (20 qualified sub-keys + 12 injection keys + 8 viewer fields + `diagram.modules`; full list in the inventory). |
| C3 | `event`: capture `.once(...)`, `_emit`/`_fire` helpers, template prefixes, constants | **Applied; two review sub-counts refused as undercounts** | Capture is now generic over member calls, helper definitions (prefix read from each helper's own fire call: none for `RE:bpmn-js/lib/BaseViewer.js:766`, `keyboard.` for `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/keyboard/Keyboard.js:179`, template `popupMenu.` for `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/popup-menu/PopupMenu.js:296`), constant/array arguments (`CLOSE_EVENTS` at `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/popup-menu/PopupMenu.js:53`) and deferred dotted-name tables/drag prefixes. Refused as stated: the review's "8" `BaseViewer` events and "5" `popupMenu.*` events undercount their own sources — `BaseViewer` emits 10 distinct names (also `import.parse.complete` at line 246 and `saveXML.start` at line 437) and `PopupMenu` emits 6 (also `popupMenu.open` at line 209); all are now entries. `event` 180 → 208 (+28 net: helper/once/constant names, minus none). |
| C4 | Eliminate shared whitelists between the extractors; strengthen `verify.mjs` to `source.path` + `detail` | **Applied** | `extract-ast.mjs` now derives every perimeter from source structure and shares no list, constant or function with `enumerate.mjs` (no common function name; its only file-name-free derivations are: didi modules from `index.js` export shapes, providers from `registerProvider`/entry-method shapes, renderer maps from the `this.handlers` constructor, moddle descriptors from the moddle entry's JSON imports at `RE:bpmn-moddle/lib/simple.js:7`, service classes from didi `type` registrations, examples from README headings; the generator's own file anchors remain generator-side only). Keyboard: `KEYS_*` groups are merged into the matching action detail (no `KEYS_*` entries remain), `searchPad:ArrowLeft/ArrowRight` (`RE:diagram-js/lib/features/search-pad/SearchPad.js:153`) and `handTool:Space` (`RE:diagram-js/lib/features/hand-tool/HandTool.js:186`) are captured; `keyboard` 33 → 30 (−6 `KEYS_*`, +2 arrows, +1 hold key). API: the 16-class table is deleted on both sides; both extractors resolve every didi `type` service class plus lib-root entry classes, including constructor-assigned methods (`RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/replace/BpmnReplace.js:344`, `RE:diagram-js/lib/features/auto-place/AutoPlace.js:51`); `api` 131 → 437. Examples: both sides now key on the README heading (tombstones have none), with independent implementations. `verify.mjs` additionally compares `source.path` and `detail` for every shared key and prints both values on disagreement; tamper controls (re-sourced, re-detailed, removed, invented entries) each fail naming the exact key. The strengthened cross-check also exposed a generator bug the review had not listed — `toggleElementCollapseBehaviour :` with a space before the colon (`RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/modeling/behavior/index.js:134`, same shape as R1's `ReceiveTask`) — now counted in the `module` detail. |
| C5 | Fix `behaviour`/`acceptance`/`proof` texts; regenerate; update spec totals | **Applied** | `popup-menu` acceptance now distinguishes provider (`open provider …`), header entry (`toggle header entry …`) and menu entry (`activate entry …`) by the entry detail; `palette` `tool-separator` (separator at `RE:bpmn-js/lib/features/palette/PaletteProvider.js:163`) states it creates nothing and its acceptance asserts a non-interactive divider; `keyboard` behaviour/acceptance distinguish search-pad keys and the hand-tool hold key from editor-action bindings. Proofs: `Canvas.viewbox/scroll/zoom` now point at `WT:packages/diagram-canvas/src/transform.ts:200` (camera transform) and `Canvas.addShape/getRootElement(s)/addConnection/removeShape/removeConnection` at `WT:packages/diagram-canvas/src/scene.ts:168` (scene construction); no entry points at `hit.ts:85` any more (point/region hit test only) and the unused `hit` proof helper was removed from the generator. Inventory regenerated (910 → 1237: `api` +306, `event` +28, `keyboard` −3, `config` −4, details-only fixes elsewhere) and §3–§6/§9 totals updated to match. |

No round-2 correction required touching `.track/`, and none was applied to shared docs or registration files.

